# Local development credentials.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `bun run dev` loads this file for apps/api, apps/cli and apps/web (LOB-256); a variable exported in
# the shell wins over it.
#
# The Anthropic credential (LOB-258). @earendil-works/pi-ai reads it itself, and apps/api picks the
# anthropic backend when any of these resolves. Set ONE; pi-ai tries them in this order:
#   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN   a bearer token, sent as `Authorization: Bearer` (a gateway or proxy token)
#   ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_TOKEN  sent as the API key
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY      an Anthropic Console API key: the usual choice
# or workload identity federation, which needs all three of
#   ANTHROPIC_FEDERATION_RULE_ID, ANTHROPIC_ORGANIZATION_ID, ANTHROPIC_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE
# (ANTHROPIC_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID and ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID optional beside them).
# An empty or whitespace-only value counts as unset. The boot log names the variable that
# authenticated (`model backend: anthropic (auth: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)`), never its value.
#
# Not supported: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN and a Claude Pro/Max login. pi-ai does not read the
# former, and the API keeps no stored login for the latter; a subscription is one person's seat,
# not a credential for a service that runs sessions unattended. The boot says when
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is set and nothing else is.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# GitHub token for the control plane's own calls to GitHub (push, PR creation). It is never given
# to a session's directory or environment. Unset: those calls fail with a typed "missing" error.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
#
# Or the GitHub App flow (LOB-55): set all three, and leave GITHUB_TOKEN unset. The App mints a
# short-lived installation token per repo. GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY is the PEM; literal \\n is accepted.
# GITHUB_APP_ID=
# GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# GITHUB_APP_INSTALLATION_ID=
# GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com

# Local Postgres from `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (the default, so usually unset).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://factory:factory@localhost:5442/factory

# Which model sessions run against (apps/api). Unset: anthropic when an Anthropic credential above
# resolves, otherwise pi-ai's deterministic faux provider, which runs sessions offline with scripted
# answers. `anthropic` with no credential refuses to boot (AnthropicCredentialMissing) rather than
# failing on the first request.
# MODEL_BACKEND=anthropic

# Where a session's working directory is created, one directory per session. Local-dev scratch
# until M6 gives each session a git worktree.
# SESSION_ROOT=.factory/sessions

# Release a session's owner (and its in-memory fold) after this long untouched. A read counts as
# use. Sweeps run at least twice per window.
# SESSION_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=900000

# Inbound triggers (`packages/core/src/TriggerService.ts`, apps/api's `/webhooks/*`). A route with
# no secret refuses every delivery with 503, so a delivery can never start a session unsigned. The
# rules map an event's label to a repo, a base ref, and a prompt template:
#   TRIGGER_RULES=[{"label":"factory","repo":"owner/name","baseRef":"main","prompt":"Work on {{title}}: {{body}}"}]
# TRIGGER_SECRET=            # hmac-sha256 secret for /webhooks/generic
# TRIGGER_SECRET_HEADER=     # header the signature arrives in (default x-trigger-signature)
# TRIGGER_DELIVERY_HEADER=   # header carrying the delivery id (default x-trigger-delivery)
# TRIGGER_MAX_BODY_BYTES=    # cap on a delivery body (default 65536)
# LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=     # Linear's webhook signing secret, for /webhooks/linear
# SENTRY_CLIENT_SECRET=      # the Sentry integration's Client Secret, for /webhooks/sentry
# SENTRY_RATE_LIMIT=         # Sentry deliveries that can start work admitted per window, per process (default 20)
# SENTRY_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS= # the window SENTRY_RATE_LIMIT counts over (default 60)
# Linear write-back (`packages/core/src/LinearSync.ts`, LOB-15): a delegated issue moves to the
# started state when its session opens, gets its PR (an attachment and one comment with the
# verification evidence) and moves to in review when the PR opens, gets one comment when a run ends
# without a PR, and moves to done when the PR merges. No key: no write-back.
#   LINEAR_API_KEY=                      # a personal API key, sent as-is; an OAuth token as "Bearer <token>"
#   LINEAR_STATE_STARTED=In Progress     # the team's workflow state names (these are the defaults)
#   LINEAR_STATE_IN_REVIEW=In Review
#   LINEAR_STATE_DONE=Done
#   LINEAR_SESSION_URL_BASE=             # optional: where a reader finds a session, for the comment
#   LINEAR_API_URL=                      # optional: the GraphQL endpoint (default Linear's own)
#   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=               # the secret of a GitHub `pull_request` webhook at /webhooks/github:
#                                        # a merge moves the issue to done, an unmerged close comments
#   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_MAX_BODY_BYTES=       # cap on a /webhooks/github body (default 1048576)
# The docs trigger (`packages/core/src/DocsTrigger.ts`, LOB-197/LOB-234). The same GitHub webhook,
# subscribed to `push` too, starts one docs run on `factory/doc-<push>` for each push to a
# registered repo's default branch (GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET above; a push to any other branch is 400).
# The schedule starts one per interval over one registered repo; unset, there is no schedule.
#   DOCS_SCHEDULE_MS=                    # the interval in milliseconds (unset or 0: off)
#   DOCS_SCHEDULE_REPO=                  # owner/name; required when DOCS_SCHEDULE_MS is set
# Jira adapter (`packages/core/src/Jira.ts`, LOB-189). All three of the base URL, the account's
# email and its API token are needed together: `jiraConfigFromEnv` answers "no adapter" unless all
# three are set, so a deployment that sets none has no Jira adapter and one that sets a partial
# config is the same as none — the adapter is not built from half a credential.
#   JIRA_BASE_URL=https://owner.atlassian.net
#   JIRA_EMAIL=agent@example.com         # the account the token belongs to (Basic auth)
#   JIRA_API_TOKEN=                      # Jira Cloud API token
#   JIRA_SESSION_URL_BASE=               # optional: where a reader finds a session, for the comment

# Send OTLP logs and traces to a local motel server (https://github.com/kitlangton/motel).
# Unset: the apps and CLI ship no telemetry at all, which is right for every run that is not
# being debugged. Set it, then read what arrives with `bun run motel`:
#
#   MOTEL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:27686
#   OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=factory-api   # default: factory-api for apps/api, factory-cli for apps/cli
#
# See tools/motel/README.md for the scripts and .pi/skills/motel-debug for how to query it.
